WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.128
Selling is allowed.

00:00:01.128 --> 00:00:02.256
Lying is not.

00:00:02.256 --> 00:00:03.760
Your reputation is inventory.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.392
This lesson is about ethics of selling.

00:00:06.392 --> 00:00:08.648
No fake scarcity or fake testimonials.

00:00:08.648 --> 00:00:11.280
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.040
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:20.680
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:24.816
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.816 --> 00:00:29.328
Stay practical: write your ethics line before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:29.648 --> 00:00:30.763
No fake scarcity.

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:31.877
No fake testimonials.

00:00:31.877 --> 00:00:34.478
No hiding what the offer cannot do.

00:00:34.478 --> 00:00:37.079
Remember the objective: write your ethics line.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:41.166
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:41.166 --> 00:00:45.624
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.624 --> 00:00:49.711
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:49.711 --> 00:00:54.169
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.169 --> 00:00:56.770
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:58.256
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:58.576 --> 00:01:02.319
Be clear on price, delivery, and who it is for.

00:01:02.319 --> 00:01:03.442
Clarity is kindness.

